        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: తూకం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తూకం (tūkaṁ) — \"weight\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తూకం (tūkaṁ) is weight — what the scales say, and also the act of weighing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Almost everything in an అంగడి (aṅgaḍi) is sold by it: బియ్యం, ఉప్పు, చక్కెర, మిరప. The ధర (dhara) you are quoted is a ధర (dhara) for a తూకం (tūkaṁ), so the two words travel together."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It carries fairness as well. Somebody who speaks with తూకం (tūkaṁ) is somebody whose words are measured, and short తూకం (tūkaṁ) is a serious accusation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four. What the ధర (dhara) is attached to."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
