      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:8fec672bd7e3808a",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did tūkaṁ mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: బేరం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "బేరం (bēraṁ) — \"a bargain, haggling\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "బేరం (bēraṁ) is the haggle — the back and forth between the ధర (dhara) asked and the ధర (dhara) paid, and also the deal that comes out of it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is expected in an open market crowd and out of place in a fixed-price అంగడి (aṅgaḍi), and telling those two apart is most of what a newcomer gets wrong."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "However the బేరం (bēraṁ) ends, it ends with ధన్యవాదములు, and in a small అంగడి (aṅgaḍi) it ends with both sides fairly sure they did well out of it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: అంగడి (aṅgaḍi), డబ్బు (ḍabbu), ధర (dhara), తూకం (tūkaṁ), బేరం (bēraṁ). Enough to buy something and thank the person who sold it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
